    "findings": [
      "Release dependency advertises enabled defaults for ticker registration map, native collision intersection, and border gate. Individual mixins were read only from local JAR bytes.",
      "collections.block_entity_tickers replaces the LevelChunk tickersInLevel lookup map with an Object2ObjectOpenHashMap. This cannot establish a change in the independent ServerLevel entity-before-block-entity dispatch.",
      "The compiled border gate still consults world border, BLOCK_TICKING and areEntitiesLoaded. A known core BE in a loaded chunk therefore supplies weaker evidence than a core eligible to tick.",
      "The optimized noCollision path is relevant to WeaponLift clearance. It does not supply an attack-contact point; the ground-support authoring still uses Level.clip. Current runtime activation and actual native geometry remain unobserved."
    ]
